From: gt510 <gt510@localhost>
Subject: media: venus: vdec: submit capture buffers restarted during a seek

GStreamer's v4l2 decoders seek with STREAMOFF on both queues, then
STREAMON on CAPTURE first and OUTPUT second. vdec_start_capture() returns
early while the output queue is off, so the capture buffers queued before
STREAMON stay in the m2m context and streamon_cap stays 0. When OUTPUT is
restarted in the SEEK state, vdec_start_output() only queues the DPB
buffers, and only if streamon_cap is set. Decoders without a separate DPB
(single output, e.g. Venus 1.x on MSM8916) then have no buffer to decode
into: the firmware stops consuming input and the pipeline never finishes
the seek. On SM-T550 every GNOME Showtime start (it seeks after preroll)
froze on the first frame; a flushing seek in playbin3 never completed.

When the capture queue is streaming but was never started by the driver,
do what vdec_start_capture() deferred: queue the DPB buffers, submit the
pending capture buffers and mark capture as started.

---
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/vdec.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/vdec.c
@@ -1127,6 +1127,25 @@
 				ret = venus_helper_queue_dpb_bufs(inst);
 				if (ret)
 					return ret;
+			} else if (vb2_is_streaming(v4l2_m2m_get_dst_vq(inst->m2m_ctx))) {
+				/*
+				 * The capture queue was restarted while the output
+				 * queue was off (a seek: STREAMOFF both, STREAMON
+				 * capture, STREAMON output), so vdec_start_capture()
+				 * returned early and its buffers are still waiting in
+				 * the m2m context. Hand them to the firmware now: a
+				 * decoder without DPB buffers decodes straight into
+				 * them and otherwise stalls for good.
+				 */
+				ret = venus_helper_queue_dpb_bufs(inst);
+				if (ret)
+					return ret;
+
+				ret = venus_helper_process_initial_cap_bufs(inst);
+				if (ret)
+					return ret;
+
+				inst->streamon_cap = 1;
 			}
 		}
 		goto done;
